          <Pad Id="3sYROub7a9zMPweo2NtwTy" Bounds="85,915,830,305" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- The circles are Point nodes, defined in this patch (Circle, Drag and Translate): one Point in a ForEach per shape. Their Position outputs, the centres of the circles, are the Points of the Polygon, so dragging a circle reshapes it. Translation sets the start positions, Radius the size of the circles.&#xD;&#xA;- Both pentagrams share the same draggable points: the second Polygon gets the same Points and is moved to the right by a Transform (TransformSRT), so dragging a circle changes both. The circles sit on the first pentagram.&#xD;&#xA;- Points are in units of the Renderer Space (1 unit = 100 DIP, origin top left), in the space of the parent. Transform acts around the origin of the parent.&#xD;&#xA;- Fill Rule decides which areas of a self-intersecting outline count as inside: NonZero fills every area the outline encloses at least once, EvenOdd leaves out the areas enclosed an even number of times, here the centre of the pentagram.&#xD;&#xA;- A Polygon is filled by default and has no stroke (Stroke Width 0). Defaults follow Skia: Join Miter, Fill Rule NonZero (Skia: Winding).&#xD;&#xA;- Points that change every frame cost real time: stay below about 4000 points, or move the shape with Transform instead.&#xD;&#xA;- Connect it to Renderer [Qt] or a Group [Qt].">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
        </Canvas>
